BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jizo Peace Project  — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, Californi
 a
DTSTART:20260807T000000
DTEND:20260808T000000
UID:736f0807388ffa310a933f48c6c1b613@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Jizo Peace Project: Clay Gathering for Remembrance and Peace\,
  August\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $10.00\n        \n      \
 n    \n  \n\nFriday\, August 7\, 2026\; 1:30 – 4:00pmDue to limited capa
 city\, we are asking for a suggested donation of $10 to the Sebastopol Cen
 ter for the Arts to confirm your attendance. Bring a copy of your receipt 
 at check-in to Painting/Drawing Studio adjacent to Ceramics Studio. Additi
 onal donations are welcome at the time of the class to cover rental and ex
 penses for the peace project. Join us for a monthly\, heart-centered gathe
 ring where we come together to create Jizo guardians out of clay—symbols
  of compassion\, protection\, and peace. Rooted in the Buddhist tradition 
 and echoed across many cultures\, Jizo figures traditionally honor childre
 n and all who have passed\, those in transition\, and those in distress.Th
 is ongoing project is dedicated to remembering those lost to war\, with a 
 special focus now on the approximately 19\,000 children who have perished 
 in Israel and Gaza in recent years. Through the simple\, meditative act of
  working with clay\, we create benevolent beings that will become part of 
 public exhibits and peace sites\, offering spaces for reflection\, mournin
 g\, and hope. Our gatherings conclude with a gentle ritual to honor the li
 ves of these children.Located in the Painting & Drawing Room. The gatherin
 g is open to ages 12 - adult\, and no prior clay experience is necessary
 —all clay and basic materials are supplied. Registration is required to 
 participate.Donations are welcome to help cover materials and expenses. Mo
 re than a class\, this is a shared space of warmth and care—an opportuni
 ty to tend to our own hearts while taking part in love in action.\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n     
        \n              \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
