DESCRIPTION:Studio Practice: Mother Mandala\n\n  \n    \n      \n      fro
 m $10.00\n    \n  \n\nOpen to mothers of all ages\, this Studio Process wo
 rkshop will offer participants the opportunity to forge art works in an ex
 periential group setting. Through a series of hands-on creative prompts\, 
 the class explores\, de-stigmatizes\, and shifts the mothers' experience i
 nto a creative framework. Together\, the individual pieces will produce a 
 unique and evanescent Mother Mandala\, at once reflecting and embodying ou
 r individual and collective maternal knowledge. No experience required\; a
 ll materials will be provided. Class participants limited to 12.  Kris Ma
 lone Grossman holds a BA from UC Berkeley and an MFA from Sarah Lawrence C
 ollege. Her work has recently appeared in FemSpec\, Re/Vision\, The Interd
 isciplinary Journal of Partnership Studies\, and the S/HE Divine Studies C
 onference. As part of her doctoral research in Women’s Spirituality at t
 he California Institute of Integral Studies\, she collaborated with eleven
  women artists\, from painters to dancers to filmmakers and more\, to expl
 ore how women in menopause engage creativity. A mother of three\, she will
  publish her dissertation\, “Wise Blood: Women\, Menopause\, and Creativ
 ity\,” in the fall of 2026. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                  Tickets:\
 n                \n\n\n\n                      Select Tickets\n           
          \n$10.00\n$20.00\n$35.00\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
