BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Observational Watercolor: Painting Produce (6 session series)  —
  Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260809T000000
DTEND:20260810T000000
UID:1ed111778f1d2a7d2f343b26d1cb8261@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Observational Watercolor: Painting Produce (6 session series)\
 n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $330.00\n        \n      \n    \n
   \n\nThis 6 session series meets Midday on Sundays\, starting August 9th.
  August 9th\, 16th\, 23rd (skipping August 30th)\, September 6th\, 13th\, 
 20th from 1:00pm to 4:00pm. $300.00 + $30.00 Materials Fee Age restricted 
 to 18+In this six session course\, students will learn a unique approach t
 o watercolor\, intended to address the frustration that many feel with thi
 s challenging medium. The class will focus on strengthening one’s observ
 ational skills\, while learning a watercolor technique that teaches the ar
 tist to see value and color. Throughout the course\, we will work on 3 pa
 intings\, progressing through simpler to more complex forms. With a mix of
  demonstrations and individualized instruction\, students of all experienc
 e levels will develop new skills and have a meaningful creative experience
 . Our unifying subject will be seasonal produce - fruits\, vegetables\, a
 nd herbs. These subjects are great for beginners and master painters alike
 \; their organic shapes are forgiving drawing subjects\, but their beauty 
 can be a muse for life. Instructor Hannah Day is a passionate produce lov
 er and botanical painter and will share her unique approach to rendering b
 otanicals. This class will work from life\, practicing observational drawi
 ng\, in addition to watercolor technique. With six class sessions\, parti
 cipants will have the opportunity to develop their skills and build muscle
  memory with a medium that often feels like it has a mind of its own. Beg
 inning artists and repeat students are welcome.About the Instructor: Hanna
 h Day received her BA in Visual Arts with an emphasis on drawing and print
 making from University of San Diego\, then attended University of Hawaii a
 t Manoa to receive her MFA in printmaking. Hannah’s etchings have been i
 nternationally shown and collected\, but her art practice also includes pa
 per cutting\, graphite\, and watercolor. She has taught all ages in many m
 ediums. These days\, Hannah primarily teaches watercolor\, observational d
 rawing\, and paper cutting. You can view her work at www.hannahdrawstrees.
 com  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  
         \n            \n              \n                Add to cart
