UID:27b8f0d068c77ec0b8267d116e36cc40@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:August Plein Air Tree Observational Workshop At Ragle\n\n  \n 
    \n      \n        \n          $85.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nAug
 ust 15th: 10:00am-2:00pm$75.00 + $10.00 Materials Fee Age Requirement: 18+
 In this one-day workshop\, students will learn and practice foundational d
 rawing techniques while sketching the beautiful Trees at Ragle Park. Each 
 student will choose a tree to draw\, and then spend time rendering their s
 ubject while receiving instruction in proportion and other key drawing ski
 lls. Once students have an established drawing\, they will explore the li
 ght and shadow on their tree with watercolor. Discover the meditative ben
 efits of plein air art practice\, hone your drawing skills\, and gain a de
 eper appreciation for the natural world around you through close observati
 on and intentional rendering. All materials are provided and all experienc
 e and skill levels are welcome!About the Instructor: Hannah Day received h
 er BA in Visual Arts with an emphasis on drawing and printmaking from Univ
 ersity of San Diego\, then attended University of Hawaii at Manoa to recei
 ve her MFA in printmaking. Hannah’s etchings have been internationally s
 hown and collected\, but her art practice also includes paper cutting\, gr
 aphite\, and watercolor. She has taught all ages in many mediums. These da
 ys\, Hannah primarily teaches watercolor\, observational drawing\, and pap
 er cutting. You can view her work at www.hannahdrawstrees.com  \n\n\n\n\
