 20 Sliding Scale for Workshop Join us for an evening of spoken word poetry
  here at the Sebastopol Center for the Arts! Students of all walks of life
 \, abilities\, and experience writing poetry\, or spoken word poetry\, are
  encouraged to join. Students will engage in a freewrite\, poetry reading\
 , discussion\, and structured writing with a voluntary shareout. After the
  one hour workshop\, Poetry Lives! will act as an Open Mic night open to a
 ll to read their completed\, or previously completed\, poems. Click here 
 to RSVP to just the Open MicPoetry Lives! is a monthly poetry workshop and
  open mic series that aims to create a space for anyone and everyone to co
 me\, learn more about poetic craft\, and share their poetry. The event sta
 rts with a facilitated hour-long workshop dedicated to learning craft elem
 ents\, discovering new poets\, and generating new work. Once the workshop 
 concludes\, we will hold a hosted open mic for anyone who wishes to share.
  It is not mandatory to participate in the workshop to be a part of the op
 en mic or vice versa. This event is all ages\, but that doesn't necessaril
 y mean family-friendly\, as poets are known to cover mature and adult topi
 cs from time to time. About the Poet: Jordan Ranft (He/Him) is a writer a
 nd therapist from Northern California. He has been nominated for a Pushcar
 t and Best of the Net. His poetry has been published or is forthcoming in 
 Boulevard Magazine\, Frontier Poetry\, Poetry Online\, Bear Review\, Iron 
 Horse Literary Review\, and elsewhere. His first chapbook\, Said the Worms
 \, was published in June 2023 by Wrong Publishing. He is currently working
  on a second chapbook and full-length collection. Instagram: @Jordan_Ranft
